course: dictionary
lesson: 134
title: Advertise: telling the world
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To advertise means to tell lots of people about something so they will buy it, use it or come to it. Shops advertise on TV, on posters and online, and a new drink may be advertised with a catchy song.
explain: The word works for jobs too. If a club needs a coach, it advertises the job: it tells people the job is free so they will apply. Advertise can also mean to make something known, as in «don't advertise that you're home alone», which warns you not to tell strangers something private.
explain: Writers sometimes use advertise in a playful way. «Every flower advertises to its own customers» means flowers show off their colours, shapes and scents so that bees, moths and flies come to them. Context tells you the meaning, even though the flower is not really selling anything.
fact: Advertise means to tell people about a product, event or service so they will buy it or come to it.
fact: To advertise a job is to tell people it is free so they will apply for it.
fact: «Don't advertise that you're home alone» means don't make it known to other people.
fact: «Product placement is when companies pay to show their products in films and shows; it is advertising hidden in entertainment.»
fact: Safety tip: do not advertise personal details online, such as your address or school.
exercise: Shops «advertise their sales on TV and posters.» What does advertise mean here? | Hide something from everyone | Write a long story | *Tell people about something so they will buy it | Sell a house to a family
exercise: A café needs a new cook, so it advertises the job. What does this mean? | Makes the job cheaper | Gives the job to a friend without telling anyone | Closes the café for the day | *Tells people the job is free so they will apply
exercise: «Don't advertise that you're home alone.» What does this warn you to do? | Put a sign on your door saying you are home | Shout your name in the street | *Not to make it known to strangers | Tell your teacher about your day
test: Product placement is when companies pay to show their products in films and shows. Is this advertising? | *Yes, it is advertising hidden in entertainment | No, it is a school lesson | Only if the film is a cartoon
test: A school wants a new teacher, so it advertises the job. What does this mean? | *It tells people the job is free so they will apply | It gives the job to the head teacher's friend | It closes the school for the year
exam: «Every flower advertises to its own customers: bright colours and runway lines for bees.» What does advertises mean here? | Stops working | *Shows off to attract visitors like bees and moths | Grows slowly | Hides from insects
